  LICENCE NOTE FOR THIS PROJECT

  The complete, canonical terms are the GNU Affero General Public
  License version 3 (AGPL-3.0) as published by the Free Software
  Foundation.  The verbatim text is reproduced in full at the URL above
  and is incorporated here by reference.

  Summary of what section 13 means for this project:

    If you run a modified version of LYNX as a network service, you
    must offer the corresponding source code of your modified version
    to the users of that service.

  Why: a search engine is infrastructure.  Publishing it is what keeps
  it that way.

  Commercial licensing

    Commercial licensing of LYNX is available from Anoneurx.  A
    commercial licence permits distribution and network operation
    without the AGPL source-offer obligation.  It does not alter the
    licence of the upstream AGPL source code.

  Third-party components

    LYNX depends on third-party open-source components under their
    own licences (Rust dependencies, npm packages, container base
    images).  Those licences continue to apply to those components.
    `cargo deny check licenses` and the dependency audit are part of CI
    to keep this boundary explicit.

